    "problem_statement": "# QR code rendering fails with certain module drawers\n\n### Describe the issue\n\nI've been trying to generate QR codes with different styled module drawers, but I'm encountering issues with some specific drawer types. When using `HorizontalBarsDrawer`, `RoundedModuleDrawer`, and `VerticalBarsDrawer`, the QR code generation fails.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nHere's a simple script that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image.styledpil import StyledPilImage\nfrom qrcode.image.styles import moduledrawers\n\n# This works fine\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(error_correction=qrcode.ERROR_CORRECT_L)\nqr.add_data(\"Hello World\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=StyledPilImage, module_drawer=moduledrawers.SquareModuleDrawer())\nimg.save(\"square.png\")\n\n# This fails\nqr = qrcode.QRCode(error_correction=qrcode.ERROR_CORRECT_L)\nqr.add_data(\"Hello World\")\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=StyledPilImage, module_drawer=moduledrawers.HorizontalBarsDrawer())\nimg.save(\"horizontal.png\")\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAll module drawers should work correctly and generate valid QR codes with their respective styles.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nWhen using `HorizontalBarsDrawer`, `RoundedModuleDrawer`, or `VerticalBarsDrawer`, the code fails to generate a QR code. The other drawers like `CircleModuleDrawer`, `GappedSquareModuleDrawer`, and `SquareModuleDrawer` work fine.\n\n### Environment information\n- Python version: 3.10\n- qrcode library version: latest\n\nI noticed this issue after a recent update. It seems like something might have changed in how the module context is determined for these specific drawer types."
